From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: No translation for scan codes above 0xff that are
 not extended.

MapVirtualKeyEx documents MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK and MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX as
taking a scan code whose high byte is 0, or 0xe0 or 0xe1 for an extended
key, and returning 0 when there is no translation; user32's test_key_map
already expects 0 for 0x011d and 0x021d. Wine translated such codes
anyway: winex11 compares only their low byte, and the generic path reads
0x100-0x2ff as its own extended-key table. A game that names its
controller's bindings with MapVirtualKeyExA(code, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK, ...)
for codes 0x100 and up (expecting 0, then its own name for the code) got
keyboard keys instead, wrote them into its bindings file, and lost its
controller bindings on the next start (Wine bug 20834).

Check it once, at the public entry, before the driver is called: the
drivers get 0x1xx codes for extended keys from inside win32u and winex11
on purpose (winex11's GetKeyNameText keeps the extended bit in the code;
win32u's map_scan_to_kbd_vkey, the keyboard input path, passes extended
keys as 0xe0xx), and every internal caller of NtUserMapVirtualKeyEx asks
a VK_TO_* mode or masks the code to 0xff. Clear the todo of the six
test_key_map rows this makes pass and add MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK rows; the
user32 tests were not run with this change (they inject keystrokes into
the session).
---
 dlls/user32/tests/input.c | 15 +++++++++------
 dlls/win32u/input.c       |  7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/user32/tests/input.c b/dlls/user32/tests/input.c
index 7e555f2aa7..d99e22010a 100644
--- a/dlls/user32/tests/input.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/tests/input.c
@@ -3294,21 +3294,24 @@ static void test_key_map(void)
         BOOL todo;
     } tests[] =
     {
-        {0x136, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
+        {0x136, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0},
         {0xe036, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
         {0xe136, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
         {0x37, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, VK_MULTIPLY, TRUE},
-        {0x137, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
-        {0x237, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
+        {0x137, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0},
+        {0x237, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0},
         {0xe037, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, VK_SNAPSHOT},
         {0xe137, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
         {0x45, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, VK_NUMLOCK},
-        {0x145, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
+        {0x145, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0},
         {0xe045, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
         {0xe145, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
         {0x1d, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, VK_LCONTROL},
-        {0x011d, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
-        {0x021d, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0, TRUE},
+        {0x011d, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0},
+        {0x021d, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, 0},
+        {0x011d, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK, 0},
+        {0x021d, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK, 0},
+        {0x0102, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK, 0},
         {0xe01d, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, VK_RCONTROL, TRUE},
         {0xe11d, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, VK_PAUSE, TRUE},
         {0x46, MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX, VK_SCROLL},
diff --git a/dlls/win32u/input.c b/dlls/win32u/input.c
index c24bbab1d4..de0853dd2f 100644
--- a/dlls/win32u/input.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/input.c
@@ -1243,6 +1243,13 @@ UINT WINAPI NtUserMapVirtualKeyEx( UINT code, UINT type, HKL layout )
 
     TRACE_(keyboard)( "code %u, type %u, layout %p.\n", code, type, layout );
 
+    /* A scan code has a high byte of 0, or 0xe0 / 0xe1 for an extended key;
+     * anything else has no translation. Drivers are called with 0x1xx codes
+     * for extended keys internally, so this is checked here only. */
+    if ((type == MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK || type == MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK_EX) && (code & ~0xff) &&
+        (code & ~0xff) != 0xe000 && (code & ~0xff) != 0xe100)
+        return 0;
+
     if ((ret = user_driver->pMapVirtualKeyEx( code, type, layout )) != -1) return ret;
 
     if (!(kbd_tables = user_driver->pKbdLayerDescriptor( layout ))) kbd_tables = &kbdus_tables;
